<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/processes/ns#"
                  xmlns:cat-harness.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/processes/ns#"
                  id="Definitions_Process_AskThePerson" targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="1">
  <bpmn:import namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/processes/ns#" location="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/processes/ns.jsonld" importType="http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="authoring-agent" name="Authoring agent"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="user" name="User"/>
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_Process_AskThePerson">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_Process_AskThePerson" name="Ask the person" processRef="Process_AskThePerson"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_AskThePerson" name="Ask the person" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>The ONE way a question or decision is put to a person. Called as a subprocess from every step that asks; never run on its own. The rule it carries out is the box at the top of `interaction-modality`.

WHY A SUBPROCESS. The asking rule lived only in a skill, and every diagram had its own ask step with no link to it. Each enforcement was keyed to one tool name (`AskUserQuestion`), so a host with a different question tool (the Claude projects `request_decision` Decision card) asked without the rule, and the owner got bare cards with no question or options (owner, 2026-10-23: "this is PROCESS FAILURE ... maybe need better subprocess etc associations"). One subprocess, called by every asking step, makes the association visible in the diagrams and checkable.

THE ORDER IS THE RULE: the full question goes in the chat FIRST, then the card. Once answered, a card shows only the chosen option; the chat text is the only lasting record of what was asked. This holds whatever the host's own tool guidance says.

WHAT IT DOES NOT DO: decide. The caller owns the decision; this subprocess only gets an answer back to it, or the stated default when none comes.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <cat-harness.processes:policy enforcement="strict"/>
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_Process_AskThePerson">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Agent" name="Agent" partitionElementRef="authoring-agent">
        <bpmn:documentation>Composes, writes and offers the question, then acts on the answer or the default. Never treats a dismissed card as a choice.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_Process_AskThePerson</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>A_Compose</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>A_WriteInChat</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>A_OfferCard</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Answered</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>A_Record</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>A_ProceedOnDefault</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Answered</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Default</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Person" name="Person" partitionElementRef="user">
        <bpmn:documentation>Answers with one tap. Typing is never required: the person this was written for has very limited hand function.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>U_Choose</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_Process_AskThePerson" name="A question is due"/>
    <bpmn:task id="A_Compose" name="Compose the full question">
      <bpmn:documentation>What is being decided, stated as what will differ; every id, path and coined name glossed; every option with its letter, a one-line explanation and its trade-off; the recommendation, first and marked; what will happen if no answer comes. Can the reader answer without opening anything? If not, it is not ready. More than one decision open: ask the next one in full and give a count for the rest.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="interaction-modality"/>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="decision-comparison"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="A_WriteInChat" name="Write it in the chat">
      <bpmn:documentation>Post the whole composed question as ordinary chat text BEFORE any card. This is the copy that survives: a card, once answered, shows only the chosen option, and a dismissed card shows nothing. Never "see the card", never a request for a typed reply such as "1y 2n".</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="interaction-modality"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="A_OfferCard" name="Offer the same options&#10;as a tappable card">
      <bpmn:documentation>Whatever the host calls its selection tool (`AskUserQuestion`, `request_decision`, a button card): the same letters and labels as the chat text, the recommended option marked. No host card tool: say so in the chat and keep each answer to one short choice.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="interaction-modality"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:userTask id="U_Choose" name="Choose an option">
      <bpmn:documentation>One tap on the card, or any answer the person prefers to give. Free text is always available and never required.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Answered" name="Answered?">
      <bpmn:documentation>`yes` when the person chose an option. `no` when nothing came, or the card was dismissed. A dismissal is NOT an answer and never selects the default as a choice; the question stays open in the chat.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="A_Record" name="Record the answer">
      <bpmn:documentation>Hand the answer back to the calling step, quoted. If it settles how a kind of thing is decided, it is a rule: write it into the governing skill in the same turn.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="symbiotic-interaction"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="A_ProceedOnDefault" name="Proceed on the stated default,&#10;question left open">
      <bpmn:documentation>Do what the question said would happen with no answer, and say so. Nothing irreversible proceeds on a default: such a step waits for the person.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="interaction-modality"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Answered" name="Answer returned to the caller"/>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Default" name="Default taken, question still open"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Ask_1" sourceRef="Start_Process_AskThePerson" targetRef="A_Compose"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Ask_2" sourceRef="A_Compose" targetRef="A_WriteInChat"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Ask_3" sourceRef="A_WriteInChat" targetRef="A_OfferCard"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Ask_4" sourceRef="A_OfferCard" targetRef="U_Choose"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Ask_5" sourceRef="U_Choose" targetRef="GW_Answered"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Ask_6" name="yes" sourceRef="GW_Answered" targetRef="A_Record"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Ask_7" name="no" sourceRef="GW_Answered" targetRef="A_ProceedOnDefault"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Ask_8" sourceRef="A_Record" targetRef="End_Answered"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Ask_9" sourceRef="A_ProceedOnDefault" targetRef="End_Default"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_Process_AskThePerson">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_Process_AskThePerson" bpmnElement="Collaboration_Process_AskThePerson">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Participant_Process_AskThePerson" bpmnElement="Participant_Process_AskThePerson" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1180" height="380" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Agent" bpmnElement="Lane_Agent" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="80" width="1150" height="240" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Person" bpmnElement="Lane_Person" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="320" width="1150" height="140" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Start_Process_AskThePerson" bpmnElement="Start_Process_AskThePerson">
        <dc:Bounds x="232" y="152" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_A_Compose" bpmnElement="A_Compose">
        <dc:Bounds x="310" y="130" width="120" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_A_WriteInChat" bpmnElement="A_WriteInChat">
        <dc:Bounds x="470" y="130" width="120" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_A_OfferCard" bpmnElement="A_OfferCard">
        <dc:Bounds x="630" y="130" width="120" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_U_Choose" bpmnElement="U_Choose">
        <dc:Bounds x="630" y="350" width="120" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_GW_Answered" bpmnElement="GW_Answered" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="800" y="145" width="50" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_A_Record" bpmnElement="A_Record">
        <dc:Bounds x="910" y="100" width="120" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_A_ProceedOnDefault" bpmnElement="A_ProceedOnDefault">
        <dc:Bounds x="910" y="220" width="120" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_Answered" bpmnElement="End_Answered">
        <dc:Bounds x="1100" y="122" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_Default" bpmnElement="End_Default">
        <dc:Bounds x="1100" y="242" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_SF_Ask_1" bpmnElement="SF_Ask_1">
        <di:waypoint x="268" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="310" y="170" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_SF_Ask_2" bpmnElement="SF_Ask_2">
        <di:waypoint x="430" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="470" y="170" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_SF_Ask_3" bpmnElement="SF_Ask_3">
        <di:waypoint x="590" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="630" y="170" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_SF_Ask_4" bpmnElement="SF_Ask_4">
        <di:waypoint x="690" y="210" /><di:waypoint x="690" y="350" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_SF_Ask_5" bpmnElement="SF_Ask_5">
        <di:waypoint x="750" y="390" /><di:waypoint x="825" y="390" /><di:waypoint x="825" y="195" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_SF_Ask_6" bpmnElement="SF_Ask_6">
        <di:waypoint x="825" y="145" /><di:waypoint x="825" y="140" /><di:waypoint x="910" y="140" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_SF_Ask_7" bpmnElement="SF_Ask_7">
        <di:waypoint x="850" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="880" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="880" y="260" /><di:waypoint x="910" y="260" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_SF_Ask_8" bpmnElement="SF_Ask_8">
        <di:waypoint x="1030" y="140" /><di:waypoint x="1100" y="140" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_SF_Ask_9" bpmnElement="SF_Ask_9">
        <di:waypoint x="1030" y="260" /><di:waypoint x="1100" y="260" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
